# Welcome to Your Django Project!

## Getting Started

[[if .Tailwind]]- Opening this folder in VS Code auto-runs `Workspace: Start Dev`, which starts Django and Tailwind in grouped integrated terminals.
[[else]]- Opening this folder in VS Code auto-runs `Workspace: Start Dev`, which starts the Django server in an integrated terminal.
[[end]]- You can manually rerun `Workspace: Start Dev` from the Tasks menu if needed.

## Dev Startup Script
- `[[.StartScriptName]]` is generated in the project root.
- It opens a fresh VS Code window for the workspace so the auto-run task can start the dev processes.

## Admin Setup
- `[[.SuperuserGuide]]` explains how to create a Django superuser manually.
- Prefer the project `.venv` commands from that guide for manual `manage.py` usage unless you have activated the virtual environment.

## Project Structure
- `manage.py` - Django management script
- `templates/` - HTML templates when enabled
- `static/` - Static files
- `[[.ProjectDirName]]/` - Django project configuration
